      "writtenOn": "2024-09-27T04:00:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I pretty strongly disagree. The kernel/bootloader interface should really stay stable so we don\u0027t tightly tie kernel version functionality to bootloader versions. \n\nEspecially as multiple vendors are using this interface.\n\nHaving multiple version support in the kernel allows kernels to be tested and updated on devices without requiring the bootloader also be updated. It also allows for new features to be added to KABI frozen kernels without breaking things.",
      "parentUuid": "f1bc5a62_a2d3c1d4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 9,
        "startChar": 54,
        "endLine": 10,
        "endChar": 35
      },
      "revId": "38f32cbb2220e7a9274e1e40b28dc0367db9f003",
